Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 52 CLINICAL DATA  83 year old female with a left breast lump                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 5cm    95  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION PRESENT  2 INTRA DUCTAL CARCINOMA AT INKED MARGINS  SOLID TYPE  5   3 FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST AND AXILLA  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 6   90   MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definite vascular invasion is identified  Inked resection margins are negative  There is no evidence of malignancy in REMOVED_DATE lymph nodes  2 INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  10   3 ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE FOCUS  Diagnosis by  Robert B  Colvin  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 18 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm red  yellow  firm tissue mass  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm lobulated  tan nodule on cut surface extending to margin  Representative sections frozen as FX 1  saved for estrogen receptors and sent to Cox 5  Received fresh  is a 590 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm left modified radical mastectomy consisting of a 10 0cm axillary tail  an REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm skin ellipse with a 5 0cm incision superior to the nipple  The nipple and areolar complex are unremarkable  On cross section underneath the described incision  is a 4 5cm biopsy cavity that comes to within 0 5cm of the closest deep inked margin  The cavity is hemorrhagic  The tissue surrounding the biopsy is firm and white  Toward the lateral aspect of the breast  there is an area of hemorrhage not continuous with the biopsy cavity  SECTION CODE  A  remainder of the nonfrozen tissue from the frozen section  B  superior margin of the biopsy cavity  C  inferior margin of the biopsy cavity  D  anterior half of C  E  lateral margin of the biopsy cavity  F  medial margin of the biopsy cavity  G  more anterior half of F  H  skin half of I  I  representative inferior section adjacent