Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 21 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE OUT OF 3  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm carcinoma extends to the resection margin  Small foci of ductal carcinoma in situ are present within the tumor  comprising less than 1  of the total mass  Lymphatic invasion is present  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular firm ill defined tan yellow stellate area extending to the inked margin at one aspect of the specimen  This specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through F  with the lesion in A through C  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Paul Snowden Russell  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST LESION   report_end  , NOS.
