 note  BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  2  LATREAL   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in two container   Right breast biopsy  needle  1  medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast with localizing wires and X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm gritty ill defined nodule which abuts inked resection margin  Lesion to small to freeze  Representative sections in A through J with nodule in A through E   Right biopsy  needle  2 lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast with localizing wire and X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  submitted entirely in K through Q  Also received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit nuber  and  right breast biopsy  superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fibroadipose tissue  dissected and submitted entirely in R and S  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST  MEDIAL   LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  2   RIGHT BREAST  LATERAL   NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST MASS  1 PART B  RIGHT BREAST MASS  2 PART C  RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY  SUPERIOR MARGIN    report_end  , NOS.
