en sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 MAY 96 at 16 21     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh under the patient s name and unit number  are two different specimens  Labeled  left modified radical mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm mastectomy specimen including a REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm unremarkable ellipse of skin  The nipple is also unremarkable  The specimen is inked  Multiple sections through the parenchyma show a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm fairly well defined gray to tan  hard mass located in the lateral aspect  1 3cm from the deep margin  Labeled  left axillary contents is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm fragment of adipose tissue  Fourteen lymph nodes are dissected ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm in largest diameters  Sectioning discloses extensive adipose replacement of the majority of the nodes  One of the nodes shows two white distinctive areas  Section code  J  smaller lymph nodes entirely submitted K M  medium sized lymph nodes  half of each one submitted O  lymph node with white areas P Q  largest lymph node  sectioned  and representative cross section entirely submitted Gross Description by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD          